cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite the exact Gate A evidence-index digest reviewed. For a distributed copy,
  also cite the latest valid append-only receipt that binds its Git commit and
  remote readback; absence of such a receipt means transport is unverified.
title: "Reiyah: HARBOR Gate A Research Architecture"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wahnich
    given-names: Daniel
repository-code: "https://github.com/manfromnowhere143/reiyah"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.1.1
abstract: >-
  An operator-unaccepted governance-correction candidate for the static Gate A
  research architecture covering object-level human and automation belief,
  readiness, recoverability, joint silent misses, causal policy effects,
  transfer, explicit unknowns, and worst-group validation. The Gate A 1.1.0
  mission and protocol releases remain unchanged.
keywords:
  - automated driving
  - human automation interaction
  - uncertainty
  - causal inference
  - benchmark governance
